---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade"}
  description={"About: Downward LUT6 compilation in a four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade, Yosys/Verilator xck26 RTL simulation, Split-Conformal ACI gating, and AirMoL 4-bit NVMe streaming on 2026 hybrid models."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study reports the public reference at openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai (commit af152ba). It places a reconfigurable 6-input truth-table (LUT6) lookup tier ahead of Mamba-3 and 4-bit NVMe-streamed late-2026 hybrid and sparse-MoE models up to 34.66B parameters (LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, google/gemma-4-E2B-it, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B, and Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), gates commits behind deterministic verifiers, compiles certified wakes downward into 81-RAMB36E2 Beneš-routed lookup and canonical skill pages, and serves them over OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 (mol-agent).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Software, Metal shader, I/O, and reported_j measurements: Darwin F_NOCACHE os.pread NVMe byte counts and custom Apple Metal INT4 Sparse-MoE &amp; GatedDeltaNet compute shaders (holding Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B in 970.0 MB = 1.47% FP16 RAM at 6.773 J/tok dual-channel reported_j and 12.30× NVMe reduction at 100.0% exact token parity; 500.0 MB and 3.493 J/tok on LFM2.5-8B-A1B), zero-MAC Sub1Bit-LUT6 equivalence to LittleBit-2 ITQ, an 87.50% (42/48) verified pass rate with 0.00% broken commits admitted and 2.89 ms / 0.0424 J reported_j Wave-3 replay (15,401× faster than 35B) on a 48-task late-2026 coding bakeoff, and an 87.50% (14/16) verified pass rate with 0.00% broken patches on a 16-task multi-file git-repository SWE-Mini pytest suite.</li>
        <li>RTL synthesis, cycle simulation, and VCD switching-activity audit: 41,185–41,623 xcup CLB LUTs (35.2%–35.5% of xck26; 66,881–67,366 in clai_kv260_axi_top), 81 RAMB36E2 blocks (56.25%), and 0 DSP48 slices in Yosys 0.71+, with 1-cycle context switching (CPI = 1.0) and four-phase Verilator 5.054 VCD toggle-rate switching estimates at 250 MHz / 0.72 V (AMD DS925 est_j: 90.42–95.02 est_mW active and 60.41 est_mW quiescent — dropping 4.50× to 13.43 est_mW with ENARDEN clock-enable gating — on the 512-page Beneš core, and 4.89–5.52 est_mW on clai_kv260_axi_top).</li>
        <li>Oracle-free wake gate: 0.00% false crystallization risk and 1.0000 OOD AUROC on the shifted test stream via a radially regularized JEPA-EBRM Split-Conformal + Adaptive Conformal Inference gate, keeping Conformal-bounded distinct from Deterministic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: physical KV260 bitstream loading or isolated rail power in this repository (board_metered = false, measured_j = None; §4.16 switching figures are analytical est_j / est_mW excluding static leakage), Vivado post-place-and-route 250 MHz timing closure, silicon energy leadership, or full 500-task SWE-bench Verified container evaluation beyond the 48-task contract and 16-task multi-file git-repo SWE-Mini benchmarks.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/lut-adapt/mol-downward-cascade.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/lut-adapt/mol-downward-cascade.svg" alt="Four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade with downward SleepCrystallizer compilation into Beneš-routed LUT6 pages. Design diagram, not a power reading." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Four-rung cascade and downward LUT6 crystallization loop. Design diagram, not a board power reading.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/lut-adapt/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/lut-adapt/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/lut-adapt.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
